.TH LIFE-WALLPAPER 1 "October 2026" "life-wallpaper 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
life-wallpaper \- Conway's Game of Life as a native Wayland wallpaper
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B life-wallpaper
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B life-wallpaper
runs an animated cellular-automaton wallpaper on Wayland compositors that support
.BR zwlr_layer_shell_v1 .
It can manage all outputs, react to output hotplugging, and reload configuration
changes while running.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -h , " " --help
Print command-line help and exit.
.TP
.BR -o , " " --output " " NAME
Render only on the named output. By default, all outputs are used.
.TP
.B --list-outputs
Print detected output names, make/model, logical size, and scale, then exit.
.TP
.B --version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B --dump-config
Print the resolved configuration (defaults, preset, file and flags merged) and exit.
.TP
.BI --validate-config " PATH"
Parse a config file and exit non-zero on error.
.TP
.BR --once " (with " "--output FILE.png" ", " --once-size " WxH, " --once-gens " N)"
Render one frame headless to a PNG and exit.
.TP
.BI --inject " NAME " "[--at X Y] [--edge E]"
Place a pattern at start-up (or at the end of --once). \fBtext=WORDS\fR spells text.
.TP
.BR --load-scene " NAME, " --save-scene " NAME"
Named boards in \fBscenes_dir\fR; --save-scene saves on exit.
.TP
.BR --stats ", " --verbose
Status line per second / extra diagnostics on stderr.
.TP
.BI --config " PATH"
Read configuration from PATH. If omitted, the default is
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/life-wallpaper/config.toml
or
.IR $HOME/.config/life-wallpaper/config.toml .
If the selected file does not exist, the application attempts to create it from
the bundled default configuration.
.TP
.BI --preset " NAME"
Start with one of the built-in configuration presets: 
.BR default ,
.BR ambient ,
.BR matrix-rain ,
.BR neon-brain , or
.BR minimal .
Preset values are loaded first, values in an existing config file override the
preset, and command-line options override both. If a config file is missing, it
is created from the default template but does not override the selected preset
on that first run.
.TP
.BI --cell-size " PX"
Cell size in logical pixels (2 to 64; default 8).
.TP
.BI --fps " HZ"
Generations per second (0.1 to 60; default 4).
.TP
.BI --density " VALUE"
Initial and reseed population density (0 to 1; default 0.25; also sets reseed density).
.TP
.BI --rule " RULE"
Automaton rule: 
.BR life ,
.BR highlife ,
.BR daynight ,
.BR seeds ,
.BR brain ,
.BR rotate , or a rule in B/S notation such as
.BR B3/S23 .
.TP
.BI --color " COLOR"
Use age-based coloring or a fixed named color (green, yellow, orange, red, aqua,
blue, purple) or a hex color such as
.BR #rrggbb .
.TP
.B --[no-]trail
Enable or disable fading trails from dead cells.
.TP
.B --[no-]rain
Enable or disable faint hex code-rain behind the cells.
.TP
.B --[no-]overlay
Enable or disable the generation/population status line.
.TP
.B --[no-]sysload
Enable or disable CPU-load-driven speed, sparks, and heat.
.TP
.B --[no-]patterns
Enable or disable periodic pattern injections.
.TP
.B --[no-]stamps
Enable or disable periodic logo and text stamps.
.PP
The board is not wiped on a timer. When it goes calm for
.B stagnation_secs
(moving or chaotic cells below
.B calm_pct
percent of the grid, or the whole board repeating), new life is added on top of
the existing cells. The optional
.B soft_reset_secs
timer is off by default (0).
.PP
Other supported configuration keys can be set in the TOML file. See
.BR config_example/config.default.toml
for the complete list and comments.
.PP
When settled shapes cover
.B clutter_pct
percent of the grid, whole shapes are pruned instead of resetting the board.
.SS Smoothness, look and persistence
.TP
.B smooth, render_fps
Crossfade cells between generations at up to
.B render_fps
frames per second (default on, 30). Only changing cells are redrawn.
.TP
.B pause_hidden
Stop simulating and drawing while the compositor is not showing the wallpaper
(a fullscreen window on top, screen off); detected through Wayland frame callbacks.
.TP
.B cell_gap, cell_round
Pixels between cells (default 1) and rounded corners (default on).
.TP
.B persist, save_secs
Save each output's board under
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/life-wallpaper/
on exit and every
.B save_secs
seconds, and restore it at start.
.SH PRESETS
.TP
.B default
Balanced default colors and animation.
.TP
.B ambient
Slower, calmer animation with fewer visual elements.
.TP
.B matrix-rain
Green palette, code-rain effect, and status overlay.
.TP
.B neon-brain
Fast Brian's Brain simulation with a neon palette.
.TP
.B minimal
Uncluttered appearance without trails, rain, overlays, patterns, or stamps.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The configuration file is checked on each animation tick. Saving changes applies
them without restarting the wallpaper. A
.B SIGHUP
also triggers a reload:
.PP
.RS
.nf
pkill -HUP life-wallpaper
.fi
.RE
.PP
Configuration values are loaded in this order: built-in defaults, selected
preset, config file, then command-line flags. Later sources override earlier ones.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Start with the ambient preset:
.B life-wallpaper --preset ambient
.TP
Use Matrix Rain on one output:
.B life-wallpaper --preset matrix-rain --output DP-1
.TP
Use a preset and override its frame rate:
.B life-wallpaper --preset neon-brain --fps 6
.TP
Use a custom configuration file:
.B life-wallpaper --config ~/.config/life-wallpaper/work.toml
.TP
List available outputs:
.B life-wallpaper --list-outputs
.SH LIVELINESS AND LOOK OPTIONS
These can be set in the config file as
.IR key " = " value
and most also as command-line flags (underscores become dashes).
.TP
.BR local_calm_secs ", " tile_size
A tile of the board with nothing moving for this long gets new life. 0 turns it off.
.TP
.BR decay_after ", " decay_chance
Cells stuck in a still life or oscillator for this many generations die with the given per-generation chance.
.TP
.B noise_per_sec
Random single-cell disturbances per second.
.TP
.BR rule_shift_secs ", " rule_shift_gens ", " rule_shift_mode ", " rule_shift_stagger
Briefly swap to a livelier rule (B34/S23, B3/S234 or B3/S2345) on Life and HighLife boards.
In ripple mode (the default) tiles switch over ring by ring from a random tile, each for
rule_shift_gens generations, rule_shift_stagger generations apart; in global mode the whole board changes at once.
.TP
.BR fastforward ", " fastforward_speed
Run extra generations per tick while the whole board is calm.
.TP
.BR colonies ", " colony_mutation ", " colony_colors
Births inherit the majority colour of their parents (requires color = age).
.TP
.BR traffic ", " traffic_min_secs ", " traffic_max_secs ", " gun_secs
Spaceship convoys, and the lifetime of Gosper guns (0 = forever).
.TP
.B symmetry_chance
Chance that an injected soup is symmetric.
.TP
.B hypr_events
React to Hyprland workspace and window events.
.TP
.B hypr_locate
Ask Hyprland where a window is, so a closed window blooms where it was and a new one gets a halo around it.
.TP
.B clock_stamp_secs
Every so many seconds a stamp spells the local time as HH:MM (0 = off; requires stamps).
.TP
.BR audio ", " audio_sensitivity ", " audio_command
React to what is playing, from a helper process (default: pw-cat on the default output's monitor, with
parec and pacat as fallbacks) writing raw mono 16-bit samples at 11025 Hz to stdout. Off by default; read at
start-up. The helper is restarted with backoff if it exits (\fBaudio_restart_backoff\fR,
\fBaudio_restart_max_secs\fR) and stopped while every output is hidden.
.TP
.BR audio_gliders ", " audio_react
With audio on, beats send gliders (\fBaudio_gliders\fR) and/or the board lights up with the music
(\fBaudio_react\fR, no cells added). Tune the light with \fBaudio_gain\fR, \fBaudio_brighten\fR,
\fBaudio_glow\fR, \fBaudio_bg\fR, \fBaudio_flash\fR, \fBaudio_flash_ms\fR, \fBaudio_attack_ms\fR,
\fBaudio_release_ms\fR, \fBaudio_floor\fR. Bass drives glow and flash, mid the brightness, treble the background.
.TP
.BR audio_band_bass_sensitivity ", " audio_band_mid_sensitivity ", " audio_band_treble_sensitivity
Beat sensitivity of one band (a number, or master to follow audio_sensitivity).
\fBaudio_band_bass_gliders\fR, \fBaudio_band_mid_sparks\fR and \fBaudio_band_treble_noise\fR
route a band's beats to gliders, sparks or cosmic rays.
.TP
.B cell_shape
square, circle, hex or rounded (default). \fBcell_round\fR is the old alias (true = rounded, false = square).
.TP
.BR color_mode ", " color_smooth_stops
steps (default) or smooth: a continuous gradient by age through the listed palette entries.
.TP
.BR ipc ", " ipc_path
Control socket for \fBlife-wallpaper-ctl\fR (off by default).
.TP
.BR power ", " battery_threshold ", " battery_dim ", " battery_fps_scale ", " battery_disable
Low-power mode on battery.
.TP
.BR idle ", " idle_secs ", " idle_fps_scale ", " idle_fastforward ", " idle_dim ", " idle_breathe
A calmer board after a while without pointer or window activity (Hyprland only).
.TP
.BR mpris ", " mpris_player ", " mpris_artist_colors
React to the active media player through playerctl.
.TP
.B grid
square (default), hex (six neighbours, offset layout) or von-neumann (four neighbours).
.TP
.BR cursor ", " cursor_mode ", " cursor_radius ", " cursor_interval_ms
Leave cells where the pointer goes (Hyprland). cursor_mode is trail, sparkle or soup.
.TP
.BR workspace_ripple ", " audio_band_bass_bloom ", " overlay_sparkline
A ripple on workspace switches; a pulsar on sustained bass; a population sparkline above the overlay.
.TP
.BR command ", " command_interval_secs
Lines printed by the command are events (JSON objects or control-socket commands).
.TP
.BR weather ", " weather_command ", " weather_interval_secs ", " weather_palette
Tint the palette and add rain or snow from a wttr.in-style answer.
.TP
.B rule_shift_rules
Comma separated rules a rule shift may swap in.
.TP
.BR stats ", " verbose ", " scenes_dir
Diagnostics on stderr, and where named scenes are stored.
.TP
.BR breathe ", " breathe_secs
Slowly vary the generation rate by this fraction.
.TP
.BR glow ", " vignette
Soft halo around live cells; dim towards the screen edges.
.TP
.BR hue_drift ", " hue_drift_secs ", " night_dim ", " night_start ", " night_end
Slow palette hue drift and night-time dimming (local hours).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory for the default configuration path.
.TP
.B HOME
Used to derive the default configuration path when XDG_CONFIG_HOME is unset.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Reload the selected configuration file.
.TP
.B SIGINT, SIGTERM
Shut down cleanly.
.SH NOTES
Requires a Wayland compositor with the wlr layer-shell protocol. The program is
not intended for X11 sessions without a compatible Wayland environment.
